       pnminvert - invert a PNM image


SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ppnnmmiinnvveerrtt

       [_p_n_m_f_i_l_e]


DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppnnmmiinnvveerrtt  reads  a PNM image as input, inverts it black for white, and
       produces a PNM image as output.

       If the image is grayscale, ppnnmmiinnvveerrtt replaces a pixel with one of  com‐
       plementary  brightness,  i.e.  if the original pixel has gamma-adjusted
       gray value G, the output pixel has gray value maxval - G.

       If the image is color, ppnnmmiinnvveerrtt inverts each individual RGB  component
       the same as for a grayscale image.


OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       There  are  no command line options defined specifically for ppnnmmiinnvveerrtt,
       but it recognizes the options common to all programs based on libnetpbm
       (See
        Common Options ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩ .)


